# Project Walkthrough: STEM Tutor Enhancement

I have successfully updated your STEM Tutor application to match the provided designs. Here is a summary of the changes:

## 1. Dashboard (`/`)
-   **Sidebar Implemented**: A persistent, dark-themed sidebar with navigation links ([Sidebar.tsx](file:///d:/final%20year%20project/STEM/frontend/components/Sidebar.tsx)).
-   **Widgets Added**:
    -   [ActivityChart](file:///d:/final%20year%20project/STEM/frontend/components/ActivityChart.tsx#15-64): A Recharts-based area chart showing "Time Spendings".
    -   [CalendarWidget](file:///d:/final%20year%20project/STEM/frontend/components/CalendarWidget.tsx#11-38): A custom-styled calendar component.
    -   [ProfileCard](file:///d:/final%20year%20project/STEM/frontend/components/ProfileCard.tsx#5-37): A polished profile summary card.
    -   **Stats**: Homework progress and course statistics placeholders.
-   **Layout**: Refactored to a responsive Grid layout matching the reference image.

## 2. Code Editor (`/editor`)
-   **Monaco Editor Integration**: Embedded VS Code's editor engine for a premium coding experience.
-   **Pyodide Execution Logic**: Added [usePyodide](file:///d:/final%20year%20project/STEM/frontend/hooks/usePyodide.ts#12-61) hook to download and run Python code directly in the browser (Client-side execution).
-   **Design**: Implemented the "Split View" design with:
    -   **Main Editor**: White background, syntax highlighting.
    -   **Console**: Dark background, terminal-like output.
    -   **Controls**: "Run Code" button and clean header.

## 3. Learning Environment (`/blackboard`)
-   **Infinite Canvas**: Updated [BlackboardCanvas.tsx](file:///d:/final%20year%20project/STEM/frontend/components/BlackboardCanvas.tsx) to support **Zooming** (Scroll Wheel) and **Panning** (Hand Tool).
-   **Drawing Tools**: Added Pen and Eraser logic with `react-konva`.
-   **Floating Toolbar**: A sleek bottom-center toolbar for switching tools.
-   **Floating AI Widget**: As requested, the AI Assistant is now a **minimal floating orb** in the top-right corner that expands into a conversation bubble, freeing up screen space.

## Next Steps
-   **Connect Real Backend**: Currently, data (assignments, user profile) is hardcoded.
-   **Enhance AI**: Connect the "Wise Friend" widget to an actual LLM API (Gemini/OpenAI) using the `VoiceVisualizer` logic.
